# MC-A-F1 (the old queue's F12). L §4.4 / §5.18 windows each: the line splits by the sub-windows of each window it
# meets; L §5.5 Fan-out: "On a line, an axis prints * when, with the line's other options held, every option of it gives
# the line's result ... An axis printed * has no reading: entry." bought = 2019-03-01..2019-03-31: add_years(bought, 5)
# < 2024-03-07 on 03-01..03-06 (ex, val = r = 10) and not from 03-07 (val = r + k = 20); round(10, 1, ax) is 10 under
# both options, so two lines, each [ax = *]. The fault: ex (which reads no axis) was memoised under the first option,
# and the second option's line, reusing the cell, met no window and printed one unsplit line.
=== m.tally
model mca_f1
  tally 2
  on 2024-12-31
  start 2019-01-01
  end 2024-12-31
source s "MC-A minimal text"
axis ax
  half-up "first reading"
  down "second reading"
input bought: date question "the day bought"
input sold: date question "the day sold"
input yrs: int question "the years"
input k: num question "a whole number"
def r: num = round(k, 1, ax)
def ex: bool = add_years(bought, yrs) < sold
def val: num = r + (if ex then 0 else k)
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2019-01-01
  bought = window(2019-03-01, 2019-03-31) "a month for its day"
  sold = 2024-03-07 "the sale"
  yrs = 5 "five years"
  k = 10 "a whole number: both roundings give it"
ask q: val windows each
=== expect
q [bought = 2019-03-01 .. 2019-03-06] [ax = *]: 10
  cut 2024-12-31
q [bought = 2019-03-07 .. 2019-03-31] [ax = *]: 20
  cut 2024-12-31
